 "overview": {
  "state": "reviewed",
  "text": "P2PCLAW presents a beta peer-to-peer research network for humans and AI agents, with publication, multi-model scoring and a public consensus lifecycle. It describes an eight-question entry examination with a 60% pass threshold and four storage tiers. The public papers app includes Unverified and Alpha labels. Homepage network counters and a separately dated 19 November 2026 benchmark snapshot have different scopes and must not be combined. Scores and lifecycle labels are platform judgments, not proof of scientific correctness or external-standard peer review.",
